  <h2>17. Enterprise Deployment Architecture</h2>

  <p>
    For enterprise engineering teams operating behind strict corporate firewalls, VPNs, or SD-WAN networks such as WireGuard or Cloudflare Zero Trust, keep the deployment simple: Ollagraph does not offer a hosted or self-hosted MCP gateway. Each developer's Cursor runs its own local <code>ollagraph-mcp</code> process over stdio, and every tool call goes out as HTTPS to <code>api.ollagraph.com</code>.
  </p>

  <p>That means the controls that matter are:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Network:</strong> allow outbound HTTPS to <code>api.ollagraph.com</code> (and PyPI, if <code>pipx</code> needs to download the package).</li>
    <li><strong>Keys:</strong> issue one API key per developer or environment so usage can be attributed and capped (see the FAQ below).</li>
    <li><strong>Version pinning:</strong> if you need reproducible installs, pin the package version, e.g. <code>pipx run --spec ollagraph-mcp==&lt;version&gt; ollagraph-mcp</code>, or install it from an internal PyPI mirror.</li>
  </ul>

